nexus embedded binaries — e2fsprogs 1.47.2
===========================================

nexus distributes the following statically-linked binaries built from the
unmodified e2fsprogs 1.47.2 source tarball:

  mke2fs    — create ext2/3/4 filesystems
  e2fsck    — check and repair ext2/3/4 filesystems
  resize2fs — resize ext2/3/4 filesystems

The binaries are statically linked against musl libc (MIT licence,
https://musl.libc.org/). The e2fsprogs programs themselves are licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2). The full text of
the GPLv2 and the LGPLv2 (which applies to lib/ext2fs and lib/e2p) is in
the COPYING file in this directory.

Source
------

The complete corresponding machine-readable source code is the unmodified
upstream tarball:

  https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/people/tytso/e2fsprogs/v1.47.2/e2fsprogs-1.47.2.tar.xz

A copy of this tarball is also attached to the nexus GitHub release at:

  https://github.com/IniZio/nexus/releases/tag/e2fsprogs-v1.47.2

The build recipe used to produce the binaries (cross-compiled, statically
linked against musl libc) is:

  scripts/e2fsprogs/build.sh   (in this repository)

No modifications were made to the e2fsprogs source code.

